# ============================================================================
# estate.env.example -- template for the h100_validation build plane.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   1. Copy this file to a location OUTSIDE the repository.
#   2. chmod 600 on the copy -- it will hold estate identifiers.
#   3. Fill in every required value, or set it to NONE where NONE is accepted.
#   4. NEVER commit the copy. A redaction list checked into a public repo
#      publishes the estate it was written to protect (#155).
#
# Source it before building:
#   set -a; . /path/to/your/estate.env; set +a
#   bash build_h100_plane.sh
#
# Contract: UNSET means nobody decided -> build refuses with 96 (UNMEASURED,
# not clean). NONE means "declared empty". Required knobs have NO default.
# ============================================================================

# --- REQUIRED, NO DEFAULT ---------------------------------------------------

# The filesystem root the launcher must stop hard-coding (#123).
# The build rewrites every occurrence of this literal out of the launcher,
# so it is the exact path text as it appears in the upstream launcher.
# NONE is NOT accepted here: this is the thing being removed.
# Leave EMPTY until you fill it in: an empty value still trips the required
# guard and refuses 96, whereas a <placeholder> would satisfy it and let the
# build run against a root that does not exist.
FS_ESTATE_ROOT=

# The Slurm partition name being REMOVED from the launcher (#152).
# Set it to the literal partition string as it appears in the snapshot.
# It also expands anchors in h100/fix_113.json and in three patch stages whose
# before-text names it (#157).
# NONE = this estate's launcher names no partition literal to remove.
FS_PARTITION_LITERAL=""

# |-separated regex ALTERNATION of this estate's identifiers: node names,
# account ids, org segments, private hostnames, management IPs. This is an
# INPUT (not a checked-in file) on purpose.
# NONE = declared: there is nothing to pattern-redact.
FS_ESTATE_IDENT_PAT=""

# |-separated additional branches for identifiers the pattern above cannot
# safely express, e.g. a bare account id where the regex [0-9]{5} would also
# match line counts and half the corpus.
# NOT a literal-match list: this is appended to the SAME extended regex with a
# `|`, so metacharacters are live. Escape any you mean literally -- an
# unescaped `.` matches any character and quietly widens the blocklist.
# NONE = declared: no extra branches are needed.
FS_REDACT_EXTRA=""

# --- OPTIONAL BUILD KNOB ----------------------------------------------------

# Interpreter that has pytest installed, used by the pytest-suite gate.
# Defaults to ./.venv/bin/python if unset. If NEITHER resolves, the gate
# declares UNMEASURED (95) rather than silently skipping -- it will not pass
# a check it did not run.
FS_PYTEST=""

# --- NOT SET HERE: runtime knobs --------------------------------------------
# The following are read by the GENERATED launcher at launch time, not by this
# build, and therefore do not belong in this file's required set. Required
# no-default ones fail closed at their point of use: FS_PARTITION,
# FS_ALLOCATION, FS_CONTAINER_RUNTIME, FS_ALLOWED_NODE,
# FS_ALLOWED_PATH_ROOTS, FS_CHECKPOINT_ADJUDICATORS, FS_ENGINE_LAUNCH_CMD.
# Others: FS_FORBIDDEN_NODES (deny-first), FS_BIND_PATHS,
# FS_EXTRA_BIND_PATHS, FS_GPUS_PER_NODE, FS_WALLTIME, FS_ITERATION_BUDGET,
# FS_EARLY_SAVE_STEPS, FS_PYTHON, FS_CONTAINER_SQSH, FS_NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME,
# FS_NCCL_IB_HCA, FS_NCCL_NET_PLUGIN, FS_PHASE, FS_BACKEND.
#
# NOTE the deliberate pair: FS_PARTITION_LITERAL above is the build input
# being deleted; FS_PARTITION is the operator input that replaces it. Do not
# collapse them. See h100/LAUNCH.md before launching.
